Part 1 - Understanding the Business Problem

1. What is the business problem?
The business problem is detecting fraudulent credit card transactions while still allowing the valid transactions to go through. Financial
companies process many transactions on a day to day basis making it difficult to go through every individual transaction and detect possible
fraud. Fradulent transactions are also more uncommon than legitimate transactions making them much harder to identify. AI and machine
learning could help identify patterns in transaction data and flag any suspicious transactions for more in depth review.

2. Why is the problem important to the organization?
Fraud detection is crucial because these fradulent transactions could cause losses for both the financial companies and their customers. An
institution needs to identify any suspicious activity first before any additional fradulent transactions occur. At the same time, it is also
crucial to not incorrectly flag too many legitimate purchases as fraud since that can be an inconvenience to the customers. An effective 
fraud detection system can help an organization reduce financial risk while also protecting their customers. AI usage could make this 
process more efficient by analyzing large amounts of customer transaction data faster than analyzing them individualy. 

3. Who is affected by this problem?
The main groups affected by credit card fraud are financial companies, their customers and employees. Customers can be affected when
unauthorized purchases are made using their credit cards and when valid transactions are incorrectly flagged. Fraud prevention teams are
responsible for investigating suspicious transactions and limiting financial losses. Customer service employees might also have to help
customers resolve fraudulent charges or blocked transactions. Managers are affected because they have to balance fraud prevention, operating 
costs, financial risk, and the overall customer experience.
