Part 6 - AI Solution Summary

Business Problem
A financial company wants to identify fraudulent credit card transactions before they cause financial losses. Since thousands of
transactions can happen every day, manually checking every transaction is unreasonable as ut would be difficult and time-consuming. An AI 
system could help identify transactions that show signs of possible fraud.

Data Needed
The model could use:
- Transaction amount
- Transaction time
- Transaction patterns (V1–V28)
- Changes in spending behavior
- Transaction frequency
- Past fraud results showing whether transactions were fraudulent or legitimate

AI/ML Approach
A machine learning model could analyze past credit card transactions and learn patterns that are connected to fraudulent activity. It could
then use those patterns to examine new transactions and determine whether they look suspicious.

Type of Learning
Supervised learning would work well because the historical data already identifies transactions as fraudulent or legitimate. The model can
use these known results to learn the differences between the two types of transactions.

Model Output
Classification: Fraudulent / Legitimate
The model would classify each new credit card transaction as:
Fraudulent → Yes
Fraudulent → No

Business Benefit
The organization could use the model to identify suspicious transactions quicker. This would help prevent fraudulent purchases, reduce
financial losses, and protect customers from unauthorized activity. It could also reduce the amount of time employees spend manually
reviewing transactions.

Potential Risk
One risk is that the model could incorrectly classify a legitimate transaction as fraud and cause a customer's purchase to be blocked.
It can also fail to recognize an actual fraudulent transaction. These mistakes could lead to unhappy customers or financial losses, so
suspicious transactions might still need additional review.
